# WH40k Colony Manager — .clineignore

## Purpose: keep Cline's auto-loaded context focused on what matters

## Everything listed here is generated, derived, binary, local-only, or

## superseded — Cline should not spend context reading it, and none of it is

## needed to understand or edit the project's source. (Follows

## 10-context-budget.md: targeted reads, not whole-tree scanning.)

##

## NOTE: this only affects which files Cline loads into context automatically

## It does not prevent Cline from running git commands, builds, or tests

## --- Dependencies & interpreters (large vendor trees, never read directly) ---

node_modules/
.venv/
venv/

## --- Build & test output (regenerated on demand) ---

dist/
build/
coverage/
htmlcov/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

## --- Python bytecode & tool caches ---

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/

## --- Lockfiles (machine-generated; pyproject.toml / package.json are the

## readable source-of-truth manifests) ---

uv.lock
package-lock.json
bun.lock

## --- Secrets & local environment files — never pull into context ---

## (.env.example stays visible: it is the committed, non-secret template.)

.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.staging
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.key
*.pem
cookies.txt

## --- Local databases & runtime state (binary, low value for code context) ---

*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
/data/          # root data/ holds only colony_manager.sqlite; anchored so the
                # active frontend src/data/ (rulesData.ts etc.) is NOT ignored
backups/
exports/

## --- Generated packaging metadata ---

*.egg-info/

## --- Git object store (Cline works via git commands, not raw object files) ---

.git/

## --- Local editor settings ---

.vscode/
.idea/

## --- Binary source material (spreadsheet cannot be parsed for context) ---

[WH40k_RT] [Team RT6] Colony Sheet.xlsx
*.xlsx
*.xls

## --- Superseded documentation ---

## docs/archive/ holds ~30 wrap-ups of completed migrations. Live guidance is

## docs/.manifest.yaml + top-level docs/*.md (+ docs/UI_REQ/), used as the

## targeted-read index per 10-context-budget.md

/docs/archive/

## --- Redundant design docs (maintained for other AI tooling) ---

## Gemini_UI/ duplicates docs/UI_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md + docs/UI_REQ/; Cline should

## use the project's own docs/ copies instead of this parallel set

Gemini_UI/

## --- Legacy archived rule tables ---

## Root config_archive/ holds the superseded rule_tables_legacy.yaml; active

## rules live in config/. Anchored to root so the ACTIVE Python package

## src/colony_manager/config_archive/ (loader.py, models.py) is NOT ignored

/config_archive/

## --- Generated OpenAPI snapshot (251 KB machine-generated JSON) ---

## The source of truth for API shapes is adapters/api/.../*.py. This snapshot

## is only consumed by `npm run generate:types`; regen it instead of reading it

/docs/api/

## --- Superseded Cline rules (old rule set, auto-load excluded) ---

## .clinerules/old_rules.clinerules/ is the pre-consolidation rule set kept
## for reference/history only. It contains guidance that contradicts the
## current rules -- e.g. Bearer-era frontend auth in 07-frontend-architecture.md
## that the live rules explicitly deprecate. Excluded so Cline never auto-
## loads stale rules; authoritative guidance is the top-level .clinerules/*.md,
## .clinerules/workflows/, and .clinerules/contexts/. See its DEPRECATED.md.
.clinerules/old_rules.clinerules/
